>> title: Banana Pudding
>> category: Custards & Puddings
>> tags: banana, custard, vanilla wafers, dessert, make-ahead
>> counters: Smokehouse, Diner, Meat and Three
>> aka: nanner pudding, banana puddin, vanilla wafer pudding
>> servings: 8
>> time: 5 hr
>> slack: forgiving — the custard has to reach an actual boil, because one that never boils never sets and no extra chilling will thicken it

>> step: whisk smooth in a saucepan
Whisk @granulated sugar{3/4%cup}(150 g), @cornstarch{1/4%cup}(32 g), @table salt{1/4%tsp}, and @egg yolks{4%large}(74 g) smooth in a cold #saucepan{}.

>> step: cook to a boil, 8 min
Cook @&(~1)yolks{} with @whole milk{3%cups}(720 mL) over medium heat, ~whisk{8%min}, until it comes to a boil and thickens enough to hold the trace of the whisk.

>> step: cool 20 min off the heat
Stir @unsalted butter{2%Tbs}(28 g) and @vanilla extract{2%tsp}(10 mL) into @&(~1)custard{} off the heat, then let it ~cool{20%min} under a lid.

>> step: layer in a 2-qt dish
Layer @&(~1)custard{} with @vanilla wafers{11%oz}(310 g) and @ripe bananas{4}(sliced 1/4-in thick) in a #2-qt dish{}, wafers first, custard last, pressed to the edges so no banana meets the air.

>> step: chill 4 hr
Chill @&(~1)pudding{} for ~chill{4%hr}, by which time the wafers have gone to cake.
